<p>I'm excited to announce that I will be returning to DEF CON this year with colleague Sean Marquez to give a demo lab representing <a href="https://tetrabiodistributed.github.io/papra/">Tetra Bio Distributed's Open PAPRa project</a>. </p>

<p>This Open Source Hardware (OSHW) project is a Powered Air-Purifying Respirator (PAPR) for use as Personal Protection Equipment (PPE) with N100-level filtration against airborne threats (i.e., pathogens and particulates), designed and developed by Tetra Bio Distributed.

We will demo the DIY PAPR which you can build with 3D-printed and off-the-shelf components and talk about what we're working on next.</p>

<p>I am particularly glad to be demoing this project because last year, I contracted COVID-19 at the event, which will be far less likely now that I plan to wear the PAPRa.</p>
